# Your content, never the template's.
#
# Pulling new deckkit features into a copy you have made your own used to
# collide on exactly the files you care most about — your canon, your slides,
# your positioning. These paths are marked so a merge always keeps YOUR
# version. The engine merges normally; your work is never touched.
#
# The driver is configured by `npm run update`, which sets:
#   git config merge.keep-mine.driver true
# ("true" is a command that succeeds without writing anything, so the local
# side survives.) Without that config git falls back to a normal merge, which
# is why the script sets it before every pull rather than trusting it is there.

canon/**            merge=keep-mine
company/**          merge=keep-mine
src/content/**      merge=keep-mine
public/assets/**    merge=keep-mine

# Generated, and gitignored anyway — belt and braces.
src/styles/tokens.generated.css   merge=keep-mine
